<!--
  ============================================================================
  HYPE TONE - everything the app says to the user in this voice
  ============================================================================

  One file per coaching tone: tone_hype.xml, tone_chill.xml, tone_plain.xml.
  Every file holds the SAME slot names, differing only in the tone suffix, so a
  slot can never exist in one tone and be missing from another. Rewriting one
  character's whole personality means editing one file.

  The slot names are resolved by model/CoachVoice.java, which is the only thing
  that knows all three suffixes at once. Add a slot there and in all three files.

  WHAT VARIES AND WHAT DOES NOT
  Tone reaches the copy that READS as the app talking: state pills, headlines,
  empty states, warnings, confirmations, toasts, prompts and the Dino. It
  deliberately does not reach functional chrome - nav names, field labels, units,
  category and priority names, button verbs and content descriptions all stay
  fixed, in strings.xml. "HRS / WEEK" reading differently per tone would make the
  app harder to scan, not more personable.

  Hype is the default tone and keeps the prototype's wording verbatim, so the
  app as designed is what a user sees unless they choose otherwise.

  LITERAL PERCENT SIGNS
  Some slots contain a percent sign as prose ("100% Satiated"). Those slots are
  handed straight to setText and never passed through String.format, so they are
  marked formatted="false". Without it aapt reads "% S" as a broken format
  specifier and lint fails the build. Do not "fix" one by doubling the percent:
  %% only collapses inside String.format, so it would reach the screen as a
  literal %%. The one slot that IS formatted, harvest_toast_sub, keeps both a
  real %% and a %1$d and is deliberately left alone.
-->
